{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/how-brands-create-a-luxury-feeling/audio/main-8daa397b8abe.mp3","durationSec":331.152,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":5.82,"text":"A luxury bag can carry the same everyday things as a normal bag, yet it may cost many times more."},{"start":6.5,"end":9.98,"text":"The reason is that luxury brands sell both an object and a meaning."},{"start":10.64,"end":17.52,"text":"A useful way to understand this is through four layers: object, story, access, and experience."},{"start":18.24,"end":20.16,"text":"The object is the bag itself."},{"start":20.76,"end":24.26,"text":"The story connects it to a designer, place, or history."},{"start":24.26,"end":27.44,"text":"Access controls how easy it is to buy."},{"start":28.04,"end":31.7,"text":"Experience includes the shop, service, and packaging."},{"start":31.7,"end":34.26,"text":"Price sits around all four layers."},{"start":35.24,"end":42.48,"text":"In experiments with wine, people often judged the higher-priced wine more positively even when price was the main difference they knew."},{"start":43.28,"end":48.28,"text":"A high price can therefore act as a price signal, although it does not prove quality by itself."},{"start":49.12,"end":53.32,"text":"Together, these choices show how brands create a luxury feeling."},{"start":54.18,"end":58.44,"text":"The object layer begins with materials, craftsmanship, and design."},{"start":58.96,"end":61.64,"text":"Craftsmanship means skilled work by trained makers."},{"start":61.64,"end":69.1,"text":"Hermès presents creation and craftsmanship as central parts of its strategy, and it runs training schools for leatherwork skills."},{"start":69.82,"end":76.24,"text":"For a customer, careful stitching, smooth edges, balanced shapes, and strong parts can show time and attention."},{"start":77.06,"end":81.52,"text":"However, luxury design does not always use large logos or bright decoration."},{"start":82.44,"end":86.38,"text":"Some bags have one clean shape, one color, and only a small brand mark."},{"start":87.06,"end":89.06,"text":"This is often called quiet luxury."},{"start":89.76,"end":92.86,"text":"The design seems confident because it does not shout for attention."},{"start":93.68,"end":97.44,"text":"A simple shape may also survive fashion changes better than a short trend."},{"start":98.02,"end":100.4,"text":"The story layer gives an object a larger meaning."},{"start":101.28,"end":108.4,"text":"Louis Vuitton, for example, tells a history that begins with trunk-making and its first shop in Paris in 1854."},{"start":108.88,"end":113.96,"text":"Its early flat-topped trunks answered a real travel problem because they were easier to stack."},{"start":114.74,"end":119.84,"text":"The company still describes its modern identity through that history of craft and innovation."},{"start":119.84,"end":126.28,"text":"Stories like these link a modern bag to a place, a maker, and an earlier purpose."},{"start":127.04,"end":130.2,"text":"They can also make an original product feel different from a copy."},{"start":131,"end":139.56,"text":"A copy may have a similar shape, but it does not have the same official connection to the workshop, service, and documented history."},{"start":140.35,"end":145.12,"text":"The access layer is about scarcity, which means that something is difficult to get."},{"start":145.88,"end":152.8,"text":"A brand may make a limited number, release one color for a short time, or give early access to selected customers."},{"start":153.64,"end":162.12,"text":"Research on sustainable luxury products found that perceived scarcity could strengthen people's willingness to pay when they already liked a product."},{"start":162.54,"end":164.34,"text":"The search can become part of the excitement."},{"start":165.06,"end":169.94,"text":"A customer may wait, visit several shops, or feel proud after finding a rare design."},{"start":169.94,"end":177.66,"text":"Hermès describes its own distribution network as exclusive, and says that each store chooses a different product selection."},{"start":177.66,"end":185.04,"text":"Limited access can protect a special feeling, but it can also frustrate customers or make the brand seem controlling."},{"start":186.06,"end":189.46,"text":"The experience layer begins before the customer touches the bag."},{"start":190.46,"end":196.46,"text":"Luxury shops often use open space, careful lighting, quiet sound, and only a few products on display."},{"start":197.34,"end":201.04,"text":"Each bag receives attention instead of disappearing in a crowded shelf."},{"start":201.04,"end":210.28,"text":"Hermès says its stores use unique architecture and different product selections to create a distinct experience, and it also trains sales teams."},{"start":210.72,"end":218.92,"text":"Personal service can add another layer: a salesperson may remember a customer's taste, arrange a private appointment, or help find a special color."},{"start":219.92,"end":226.4,"text":"Finally, a strong box, soft dust bag, thick paper, and ribbon slow down the opening."},{"start":226.68,"end":232.28,"text":"The packaging protects the product, but it also turns an ordinary action into a small ceremony."},{"start":233.68,"end":235.48,"text":"Luxury also has a social side."},{"start":236.4,"end":240.84,"text":"A recognizable logo can tell other people about money, taste, or group membership."},{"start":242.06,"end":246.54,"text":"Researchers use the term brand prominence for how clearly a brand mark appears."},{"start":247.42,"end":254.32,"text":"Their studies found that different customers preferred loud or quiet branding depending on the kind of status signal they wanted to send."},{"start":255.14,"end":261.76,"text":"This helps explain why one buyer wants a large logo while another chooses a design that only fashion fans recognize."},{"start":263.24,"end":264.88,"text":"Celebrities add another message."},{"start":265.66,"end":271.7,"text":"An actor, musician, or athlete can make the same bag seem elegant, creative, young, or powerful."},{"start":272.56,"end":275.46,"text":"The customer may not only think, “I like this bag.”"},{"start":275.9,"end":278.84,"text":"They may also think, “This fits the person I want to be.”"},{"start":279.66,"end":281.84,"text":"The four layers must support one another."},{"start":281.84,"end":289.42,"text":"A beautiful story cannot fully save a badly made bag, and excellent leather may not create luxury if the service feels careless."},{"start":290.18,"end":296.38,"text":"A high price can guide expectations, but the price experiments also show why buyers should look beyond the number."},{"start":297.5,"end":307.64,"text":"Luxury can lose its power when quality falls, products become too common, staff treat customers poorly, or every design follows the same short trend."},{"start":308.46,"end":312.38,"text":"The strongest brands balance physical value and symbolic value."},{"start":313.1,"end":317.58,"text":"Physical value comes from the bag's material, design, and usefulness."},{"start":318.58,"end":323.66,"text":"Symbolic value comes from its story, rarity, experience, and social meaning."},{"start":324.7,"end":330.58,"text":"The final question is personal: are those extra meanings valuable enough for the buyer?"}],"words":[{"text":"A","start":0,"end":0.16},{"text":"luxury","start":0.16,"end":0.5},{"text":"bag","start":0.5,"end":0.8},{"text":"can","start":0.8,"end":1.02},{"text":"carry","start":1.02,"end":1.28},{"text":"the","start":1.28,"end":1.46},{"text":"same","start":1.46,"end":1.84},{"text":"everyday","start":1.84,"end":2.24},{"text":"things","start":2.24,"end":2.68},{"text":"as","start":2.68,"end":2.9},{"text":"a","start":2.9,"end":3.04},{"text":"normal","start":3.04,"end":3.3},{"text":"bag","start":3.3,"end":3.8},{"text":"yet","start":3.98,"end":4.24},{"text":"it","start":4.24,"end":4.36},{"text":"may","start":4.36,"end":4.5},{"text":"cost","start":4.5,"end":4.78},{"text":"